    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nWe can use the standard algorithm to add multiple multi-digit whole numbers.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's use the standard algorithm to compute the following sum:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 801 + 523 + 198]\n\nContent:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 8|0|1; +|5|2|3; +|1|9|8]\n\nContent:\nNext, we add the numbers in each place value (from right to left). However, this time, we need to sum three numbers in each place value, as well as any carried digits:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 1|1|1; 8|0|1; +|5|2|3; +|1|9|8; 1|5|2|2]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, [MATH: 801 + 523 + 198 = 1,522.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Adding Three Numbers Up to Three Digits\n\nExample Prompt:\nLauren is listening to some songs while waiting for a train. The duration of the first song is [MATH: 123] seconds, the second is [MATH: 182] seconds, and the third is [MATH: 157] seconds. What is the total duration of all three songs?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo find the total duration of all three tracks, we need to compute the sum\n\n[MATH: 123 + 182 + 157.]\n\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 1|2|3; +|1|8|2; +|1|5|7]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers using the standard algorithm:\n[MATH: 1|1; 1|2|3; +|1|8|2; +|1|5|7; 4|6|2]\n\nSo, we have\n\n[MATH: 123 + 182 + 157 = 462.]\n\nTherefore, the total duration of all three songs is [MATH: 462] seconds.\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 31 + 457 + 99 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 587]\nb. [MATH: 577]\nc. [MATH: 556]\nd. [MATH: 477]\ne. [MATH: 487]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 425 + 69 + 278 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 662]\nb. [MATH: 772]\nc. [MATH: 672]\nd. [MATH: 771]\ne. [MATH: 762]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Adding Three Numbers Up to Five Digits\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat is [MATH: 31,252 + 12,892 + 25,034?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 3|1|2|5|2; +|1|2|8|9|2; +|2|5|0|3|4]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers using the standard algorithm:\n\n[MATH: 1|1; 3|1|2|5|2; +|1|2|8|9|2; +|2|5|0|3|4; 6|9|1|7|8]\n\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 31,252 + 12,892 + 25,034= 69,178.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 9, 375 + 15, 761 + 62, 791 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 87, 827]\nb. [MATH: 86, 927]\nc. [MATH: 87, 727]\nd. [MATH: 87, 927]\ne. [MATH: 77, 927]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nIn a particular year, Dan drove [MATH: 13, 589mi,] Brian drove [MATH: 12, 825mi,] and Faby drove [MATH: 14, 029mi.] How many miles did they drive in total?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 41, 423mi]\nb. [MATH: 41, 433mi]\nc. [MATH: 30, 343mi]\nd. [MATH: 40, 443mi]\ne. [MATH: 31, 443mi]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Adding Three Numbers Up to Seven Digits\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: 2,078,503 + 148,450 + 1,885,047 =]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we line up our numbers:\n\n[MATH: 2|0|7|8|5|0|3; +|1|4|8|4|5|0; +|1|8|8|5|0|4|7]\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the numbers using the standard algorithm:\n\n[MATH: 1|2|2|1|1|1; 2|0|7|8|5|0|3; +|1|4|8|4|5|0; +|1|8|8|5|0|4|7; 4|1|1|2|0|0|0]\nTherefore,\n\n[MATH: 2,078,503 + 148,450 + 1,885,047 = 4,112,000.]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 3, 592, 009 + 267, 457 + 2, 405, 812 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 5, 255, 278]\nb. [MATH: 6, 365, 288]\nc. [MATH: 6, 264, 268]\nd. [MATH: 5, 265, 268]\ne. [MATH: 6, 265, 278]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nThe area of the USA is [MATH: 3, 796, 742mi^{2},] the area of Canada is [MATH: 3, 855, 100mi^{2},] and the area of Mexico is [MATH: 761, 610mi^{2}.] What is the total area of these three countries?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 8, 413, 452mi^{2}]\nb. [MATH: 7, 413, 452mi^{2}]\nc. [MATH: 8, 312, 452mi^{2}]\nd. [MATH: 7, 213, 452mi^{2}]\ne. [MATH: 6, 403, 452mi^{2}]"
